# One line ending in the repository, whatever the machine checking it out.
#
# Without this, Git on Windows warns on every `add` that it will convert LF to
# CRLF, and a file committed from one platform shows as wholly rewritten when
# touched on another. `text=auto eol=lf` stores text as LF and lets each
# checkout use whatever it likes locally.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Never reinterpreted as text.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.webp binary
*.ico binary
